        "original_id": "8c456c7b-9414-5a20-8151-6b9c6d3f0851",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ghosts, Battle for Haditha, The Hurt Locker, Redacted, Fair Game\n- People: Nick Broomfield, Kathryn Bigelow, Brian De Palma, Sean Penn\n- Concepts: Gweilo\n- Places: Jordan\n- Topics: Cinema of Jordan\n\nFacts:\n- Ghosts is a 2006 film whose title refers to the Cantonese slang term \"Gweilo\" (鬼佬), meaning \"ghost man,\" which is used for white people.\n- In its unmodified form, Gweilo applies only to people of European ethnicities and has a history of racially deprecatory use.\n- Battle for Haditha dramatizes real events in a documentary style.\n- Battle for Haditha is Nick Broomfield's follow-up to Ghosts.\n- In the context of the cinema of Jordan, Battle for Haditha was shot in Jordan and was directed by Nick Broomfield.\n- In the context of the cinema of Jordan, The Hurt Locker was shot in Jordan and was directed by Kathryn Bigelow.\n- In the context of the cinema of Jordan, Redacted was shot in Jordan and was directed by Brian De Palma.\n- In the context of the cinema of Jordan, Fair Game was shot in Jordan and starred Sean Penn.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
